      "spam": false,
      "value": "For clarification, this happens with objects that automatically drop when [Fist] is released. It does not happen with, say, the pens in the Presentation Room because you have to manually use [HandOpen] to drop them. My guess is that VR Chat automatically plays [HandOpen] after you pick up an object so that the item drops automatically when you release [Fist] (because of [Fist] never releasing 100% when you let go of the trigger for some reason). This is probably what's causing the emission of your particles that are also mapped to [HandOpen]. I'm sure there's a better way VR Chat can handle objects that drop on release...",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
